    "rawMarkdown": ">https://www.kaggle.com/code/*******/*******\n\n> Hey Claude/codex, extract any potentially useful insights from this public notebook.\n\nThat’s all you need! You don’t even need to upvote a notebook just to fork it when you’re not sure whether it’ll be useful.",
    "content": "<blockquote>\n  <p><a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/*******/*******\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kaggle.com/code/*******/*******</a></p>\n  <p>Hey Claude/codex, extract any potentially useful insights from this public notebook.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That’s all you need! You don’t even need to upvote a notebook just to fork it when you’re not sure whether it’ll be useful.</p>",
    "replies": [
     {
      "id": 3514963,
      "postDate": "2026-08-20T13:40:24.283Z",
      "rawMarkdown": "Maybe you could also ask Claude to scan the top scoring public notebooks and tell you which are original work, and which are a fork with one hyperparameter changed and a new name on it. The credits section is usually the part that got removed.\n\nThen you can decide if and who to upvote — and who to report.\n",
      "content": "<p>Maybe you could also ask Claude to scan the top scoring public notebooks and tell you which are original work, and which are a fork with one hyperparameter changed and a new name on it. The credits section is usually the part that got removed.</p>\n<p>Then you can decide if and who to upvote — and who to report.</p>",
